# Generated data files — never let git line-merge these.
#
# Both are rewritten in full by each pipeline run (src/main.py writes
# opportunities.json via json.dump, history.py writes history.json). When main
# and a feature branch each regenerate them, git's textual auto-merge happily
# interleaves records from both sides and produces invalid JSON *without
# reporting a conflict* — which silently breaks the dashboard, since app.js
# reports a JSON parse error as "Could not load opportunities.json".
#
# "-merge" forces a real conflict instead. To resolve: take either side
# (git checkout --ours / --theirs) and let the next daily run rewrite it, or
# regenerate on the spot with `python -m src.main --no-email`.
docs/opportunities.json  -merge
data/history.json        -merge
